A.1.0. {"problem": "The request says the owner sees the deadline when the decision is asked, but the change only adds an optional field to the object and the action params. Nothing declares that the owner is shown it. There is no effect, handoff or outbox rule that carries it, and no scenario checks it. The deadline is stored but the stated goal is not delivered.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.request_decision and objects.DecisionRequest.deadline", "kind": "behaviour"}
A.1.1. {"problem": "The deadline is a free string with no date type or format, and nothing happens when it passes. `decide` and the DecisionRequest transitions ignore it, so a past or malformed value is accepted silently. The 'answer in time' purpose is not enforced and can't be checked.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, DecisionRequest.deadline, actions.request_decision.params.deadline, decide", "kind": "other"}
A.2.0. {"problem": "The request says the owner should see the deadline when asked. The change only adds an optional free-text field to DecisionRequest and to request_decision's params. No effect, notification or outbox step carries it to the owner, and the description of request_decision and DecisionRequest still doesn't mention it. A deadline can be stored but nothing shows it, so the stated purpose is not met.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action request_decision and object DecisionRequest (deadline)", "kind": "behaviour"}
A.2.1. {"problem": "The deadline is an unconstrained string, not a date. Any text such as 'soon' or a past or malformed date is accepted, and nothing compares it with anything. 'Make the owner answer in time' is therefore unenforceable and the owner cannot rely on it. decide stays allowed after the deadline, and the DecisionRequest transitions and invariants say nothing about an overdue request.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, DecisionRequest.deadline and request_decision.deadline", "kind": "other"}
A.2.2. {"problem": "No fixture or scenario uses the new field. DR1 has no deadline and no scenario requests a decision with one, so the new behaviour is untested and the 'visible to the owner' claim is never checked.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, world fixtures (DR1) and scenarios", "kind": "other"}
A.3.0. {"problem": "The change adds a `deadline` field but nothing in the declaration shows it to the owner when the decision is asked. `request_decision` has no effect, handoff or notification that carries it, and no scenario checks it. The stated goal (the owner sees the deadline when asked) is not met by storing an optional value alone.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml, action request_decision and object DecisionRequest.deadline", "kind": "behaviour"}
A.3.1. {"problem": "`deadline` is a free-form string with no date type or format. A value such as 'soon' or '3/4/25' is accepted, so it can't be compared with the current date, sorted or checked. Nothing happens when the deadline passes: `decide` and the DecisionRequest transition matrix ignore it, and open requests can still stall, which is the problem the change aims to fix.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml, DecisionRequest.deadline and request_decision.params.deadline", "kind": "other"}
A.3.2. {"problem": "The new `deadline` field and param carry no source or confirmation of their own. DecisionRequest and request_decision still cite the old interview quote ('9번은 추천대로...'), which says nothing about deadlines. The fixture DR1 and the scenario a-decision-is-taken-once were not updated, so nothing exercises the new field.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml, DecisionRequest / request_decision source, world fixture DR1, scenarios", "kind": "reference"}
A.4.0. {"problem": "The request says the owner sees the deadline when the decision is asked, but the change only adds an optional free-text field. Nothing in request_decision or the DecisionRequest declaration puts the deadline in front of the owner. The description still reads 'proposed with grounds and a recommendation and sent to that person's outbox' and does not mention the deadline. The field is stored but nothing shows it, so the stated purpose is not met.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: actions.request_decision and objects.DecisionRequest (description and deadline property)", "kind": "behaviour"}
A.4.1. {"problem": "The deadline is an unconstrained string, with no date type, format or precondition. A past or unparseable value is accepted, and decide ignores the deadline entirely. An open request can pass its deadline and stay open with no effect, so the change does not make owners answer in time. No scenario or fixture exercises a request with a deadline (DR1 has none).", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: DecisionRequest.deadline, request_decision.params.deadline, scenarios (a-decision-is-taken-once), world fixture DR1", "kind": "other"}
A.5.0. {"problem": "The change request says the owner sees the deadline when asked, but the change only adds an optional free-text field. Nothing in the domain surfaces it. The description of request_decision and DecisionRequest still says only 'grounds and a recommendation sent to that person's outbox', and no effect or handoff carries the deadline anywhere the owner would see it. The stated purpose, making the owner answer in time, is not achieved.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.request_decision (description, params.deadline) and objects.DecisionRequest", "kind": "behaviour"}
A.5.1. {"problem": "The deadline is an untyped string with no format, so values like 'soon' or '3/4' are accepted. Nothing checks it or compares it with a date. Nothing happens when it passes: the decide action and the DecisionRequest transition matrix ignore it, so an overdue open request behaves exactly like one with no deadline.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, DecisionRequest.properties.deadline and request_decision.params.deadline", "kind": "other"}
A.5.2. {"problem": "The new field has no scenario or fixture coverage. The DR1 fixture and the a-decision-is-taken-once scenario never set or check a deadline, so the new behaviour is untested.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, world.fixtures DR1 and scenarios", "kind": "other"}

